From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheKit <thekit@disroot.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Feb 2026 15:30:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] linker: q: implement ELF TLS relocation support

Vendor blobs use ELF TLS (TLSDESC on arm64), which the hybris Q linker
previously could not relocate. TLSDESC is not new, but blobs rely on it
increasingly in newer ports (Android 15 and 16), so it can no longer be
ignored. Since the blobs are dlopened into a glibc process with no
bionic TCB, back bionic's static TLS with the linker's own initial-exec
storage.

- Replace the old hybris bionic_elf_tls.cpp with the imported bionic
  copy and drop the linker's bionic TCB / exe-segment layout code, which
  does not apply to hybris.
- hybris_tls_storage is an initial-exec __thread array in the linker,
  so its offset from the thread pointer is a process-wide constant.
  android_linker_init records it as g_hybris_static_tls_tp_offset and
  derives tls_tp_base for the TPREL/TLSDESC relocations. No handshake
  with libhybris-common is needed, so plain dlopen (e.g. from glvnd)
  works. Because the linker is dlopened, the array is charged to
  glibc's static TLS surplus, so keep it small: 1 KiB against the 480
  bytes over 11 modules that was the most any process wanted on a
  Pixel 9, libGLES_mali.so among them at 80. Ports needing more can
  raise GLIBC_TUNABLES=glibc.rtld.optional_static_tls.
- register_soinfo_tls reserves space per module until the storage is
  exhausted, then falls back to dynamic TLS. __init_static_tls_module
  seeds the loading thread's storage with the new module's image, and
  ranges left by unloaded modules are handed out again.
- prelink_image() keeps an existing soinfo_tls instead of replacing it.
  It can run again for a library that is already loaded, and a fresh
  soinfo_tls reads as unregistered, so every repeat used to reserve
  another range and orphan the one in use.
- Move TLS_SLOT_DTV to the historically-unused APP slot (2) and restore
  upstream bionic slot numbering so offsets hardcoded in blob codegen
  (e.g. the stack protector at slot 5) line up.
- Tolerate an uninitialized DTV in __tls_get_addr and the TLSDESC
  resolvers, since a dlopened thread may not have one yet.
